   },
   "note": "",
   "page": 8
  }
 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Shifting",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "On every LOW-to-HIGH edge of CP, Q0 takes the AND of DSA and DSB and each stage passes its content to the next, Q0 to Q1 up to Q6 to Q7."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gated serial inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "DSA and DSB feed the first stage through an AND gate. With one held HIGH the other carries the data; with either LOW a LOW enters Q0 on each clock."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Master reset",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "MR is active LOW and asynchronous: a LOW clears all eight stages and drives Q0 to Q7 LOW regardless of CP, DSA and DSB. After MR goes HIGH, the recovery time trec must pass before a rising CP edge is counted."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Timing at the serial inputs",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "DSA and DSB must be steady for the set-up time tsu before the rising CP edge and the hold time th after it."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 74HC164 has CMOS input levels; the 74HCT164 has TTL input levels (VIH 2.0 V min, VIL 0.8 V max at VCC = 4.5 V to 5.5 V)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input clamp diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Every input has clamp diodes, so an input fed through a current-limiting resistor can be driven from a voltage above VCC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "DHVQFN14 centre pad",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The exposed pad under the DHVQFN14 is not a ground pin and need not be soldered. If it is soldered, its land is left unconnected or tied to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standards",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Meets JEDEC JESD8C (2.7 V to 3.6 V) and JESD7A (2.0 V to 6.0 V)."
  }
 ],
